# Reachability baseline — see scripts/deadcode.sh
#
# Every entry here is code that nothing calls, including tests. The build fails
# when something NEW joins this list, not when the list is non-empty. Removing
# an entry (by wiring the code up or deleting it) is always safe and is the
# point of the exercise.
#
# Entries are `path/to/file.go: FunctionName`, without line numbers, so ordinary
# edits do not churn the baseline.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KNOWN DEAD — a decision is owed on each of these. Tracked in TODO.md.
#
# These are NOT accepted. They are whole features and components that were
# built, tested, and never wired: exactly the defect class this gate exists to
# catch. They are listed only so the gate can be switched on today rather than
# blocked behind deleting or wiring them. Do not add anything here to make a
# build pass.
#
# - internal/welcome: RESOLVED. Wired into interactive startup; the intro now
#   also states what Aux sends to a provider and where it stores state.
# - sidebar.go: RESOLVED. Deleted -- an entire chat sidebar component,
#   superseded by the context pane and never removed.
# - diff/patch.go: RESOLVED. The seven unreachable functions were deleted. Note
#   the rest of that file is live and drives the patch tool; only the unused
#   public API on top of it was dead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


